WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_adp_121'), 'After the fix, the API answers:

POST /submissions
HTTP/1.1 202 Accepted
Location: /submissions/sub_88

{"id":"sub_88","status":"queued"}

A reviewer proposes going back to 200 OK with the same headers and body, to avoid changing the mobile app''s status handling.

Statement: "For clients the two answers are equivalent: both are 2xx success codes, and the body already says the submission is queued."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. A 200 to a POST says the processing is finished and the body is its result, which is exactly what mobile app 3.6 assumed when it rendered "0 of 0 tests passed". 202 says the request was accepted but not completed and may still fail, and its Location points to the status resource to poll. Clients, generated SDKs, retry policies and dashboards branch on the status line; they do not search the body for a word like "queued". The misconception is that every 2xx means the same thing; the status code is the client''s next step, and the next step here is "wait and poll", not "show the result".', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_adp_121') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
