Statement: "This loop handles the 429 well: exponential backoff spaces the retries out, so it does not need to read Retry-After."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The attempts go out at about 0, 1, 3, 7 and 15 seconds - all inside the 30 seconds the server asked for - so every one of them gets 429 again, adds load to a limiter that is already saying no, and after the last 16 s sleep the loop throws, even though one request after 30 seconds would have succeeded. Backoff is a guess for when the server says nothing; Retry-After is the server telling you the answer. Use it when present (seconds or an HTTP-date), add jitter, cap the wait, and if it is long, stop and tell the learner how long to wait instead of retrying in the background. The misconception is that any exponential backoff is automatically polite.', 2, 5
